flowchart TB
  accTitle: Where the pages of the website come from
  accDescr: The Markdown files in docs/ become the pages of the website, among them a page for each feature, and read the same on GitHub; the README keeps a line and a link for each. The hook of the website makes every comment of What reporters see from the functions and texts of the package issue_assistant, and the tables of the inputs and outputs on the Reference from action.yml. Every page gets a description of its own, from its front matter or its first paragraph.
  readme(["README.md:<br>a line and a link<br>for each"]) --> markdown(["docs/*.md,<br>as GitHub shows them"])
  markdown --> pages["Features, Get started,<br>How it works, Configuration,<br>Reference, Help, Home"]
  script(["issue_assistant/:<br>TEXT and render_*()"]) --> hook
  action(["action.yml"]) --> hook
  hook["`**scripts/mkdocs_hooks.py**<br>with every build`"] --> comments["What reporters see:<br>every comment,<br>English and German"]
  hook --> tables["Reference: the inputs<br>and outputs of the action"]
  hook --> described["a description of its own<br>for every page"]
  pages --> described
  classDef source fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef code fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef page fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  class readme,markdown,script,action source
  class hook code
  class pages,comments,tables,described page
